msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gensync_README.md:73
msgid "Passed a generator"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gensync_README.md:75
msgid ""
"Wraps the generator to populate the `.sync`/`.async`/`.errback` helpers "
"above to allow for evaluation of the generator for the final value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gensync_README.md:100
msgid "Passed an options object"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gensync_README.md:102
msgid "`opts.sync`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gensync_README.md:104
msgid "Example: `(...args) => 4`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gensync_README.md:106
msgid ""
"A function that will be called when `.sync()` is called on the "
"`gensync()` result, or when the result is passed to `yield*` in another "
"generator that is being run synchronously."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gensync_README.md:110
msgid "Also called for `.async()` calls if no async handlers are provided."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gensync_README.md:112
msgid "`opts.async`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gensync_README.md:114
msgid "Example: `async (...args) => 4`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gensync_README.md:116 ../../source/gensync_README.md:124
msgid ""
"A function that will be called when `.async()` or `.errback()` is called "
"on the `gensync()` result, or when the result is passed to `yield*` in "
"another generator that is being run asynchronously."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gensync_README.md:120
msgid "`opts.errback`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gensync_README.md:122
msgid "Example: `(...args, cb) => cb(null, 4)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gensync_README.md:128
msgid ""
"This option allows for simpler compatibility with many existing Node "
"APIs, and also avoids introducing the extra even loop turns that promises"
" introduce to access the result value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gensync_README.md:132
msgid "`opts.name`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gensync_README.md:134
msgid "Example: `\"readFile\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gensync_README.md:136
msgid ""
"A string name to apply to the returned function. If no value is provided,"
" the name of `errback`/`async`/`sync` functions will be used, with any "
"`Sync` or `Async` suffix stripped off. If the callback is simply named "
"with ES6 inference (same name as the options property), the name is "
"ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gensync_README.md:141
msgid "`opts.arity`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gensync_README.md:143
msgid "Example: `4`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gensync_README.md:145
msgid ""
"A number for the length to set on the returned function. If no value is "
"provided, the length will be carried over from the `sync` function's "
"`length` value."
msgstr ""

